+# packet-plumber-terminology-audit — field notes (Phase 1 audit + Phase 2 rename)
+
+- The serialization proof is the audit's spine: PP-v2 wire format is value/layout only (numeric writers, CMD_TAG_*/EVENT_TAG_* u8 constants, declaration-order enum discriminants) — ANY identifier rename is byte-neutral; only balance.json key renames (catalog-hash fold → T1 re-bless) and rendered HUD strings (→ T2 fold candidates) move bytes. Phase 2 confirmation: the harness T2 capture path never renders the app HUD (`draw_hud`), so HUD-string renames moved ZERO T2 pixels; the ENTIRE golden impact of the rename was the catalog_hash fold.
+- Re-bless discipline bites twice: (a) edit ALL data/*.json bytes (including `_comment` strings — they fold into the hash) BEFORE `harness save`, or the goldens go stale again (I hit this: a comment edit after save changed catalog_hash a second time); (b) the splice proof (`odin run bin/splice_check` — run boot with the OLD catalog_hash in run_init) reproduces the old blessed tick-1 hash exactly — the definitive "fold is the only change" proof; pair it with a .log.bin byte-diff (old-vs-new logs differ ONLY in the catalog_hash header field) + T2 PNG byte-identity.
+- A direct-pane "proceed" after a lavish poll is NOT the per-row verdict the briefing gates Phase 2 on (state.json chat held only the agent reply; 0 prompts then — the 4 rulings were stranded as pending_prompts by a poll timeout and collected later from `~/.lavish-axi/state.json`). Out-of-band go-aheads close a no-PR phase; re-verify per-row rulings before renaming code.
