+## 2. Rename cost — serialization proof & golden impact
+
+**Why every identifier rename is byte-neutral (the serialization contract, `core/serialize.odin`):**
+
+1. **Values only, never names.** The writer emits explicit numeric fields (`w_u8/w_u16/w_u32/w_i32/w_u64/w_bool`) —
+   no field names, no type names, no strings, no reflection.
+2. **Numeric discriminators.** Command kinds serialize via the `CMD_TAG_*` u8 constants; events via `EVENT_TAG_*` —
+   a rename of a union variant or tag-constant name leaves its byte constant untouched.
+3. **Enum discriminants by declaration order.** `Strain_Level`, `Warning_Sign`, `Drop_Reason`, `Root_Cause_Kind`
+   serialize as their u8 index — renaming variants (order kept) is byte-identical.
+4. **Field names never serialize.** Renaming struct fields changes no bytes; the write ORDER is the contract.
+
+**Golden fold table — the only surfaces that move bytes:**
+
+| Surface | Rename effect | Golden impact |
+|---|---|---|
+| Comments · docs prose · GDD/stories/sprint/arch/specs | no bytes rendered | no fold |
+| Non-serialized identifiers (types, fields, procs, constants) | writer emits values only | no fold |
+| Enum variant renames (order kept) | discriminant bytes unchanged | no fold |
+| Serialized command-kind rename (`Cmd_Set_Emphasis → Cmd_Set_Weights`) | tag constant kept | no fold |
+| **balance.json keys** — `lane_presets`, `lane_queue_packets`, `default_lane_preset`, `lane_auto_reserve_ladder`, `warnings.node_strained_lead_ticks`, `warnings.pipe_pressure_lead_ticks` | catalog hash folds every catalog byte (ODN-11) | **T1 re-bless — deliberate + proven** (4.3 discipline: version-field-only splice, old catalog_hash folded) |
+| palette.json keys — `lane_express`, `lane_standard`, `lane_best_effort`, `lane_speeds`, `state_strain` | app-side colors; key rename changes no color value | no fold |
+| **Rendered HUD strings** (below) | player-visible text changes | **T2 fold candidates — deliberate, listed** |
