+## 2026-08-15 — Terminology canon: networking-first vocabulary (user ruling, phase-1 audit `packet-plumber-terminology-audit`)
+
+- **Ruling.** The player is a network engineer; the game is a networking game → **real networking terms unless the
+  software term is more accurate** (arrays, stack, pool, queue — kept) **or the word is game identity** (bundle,
+  demolish, severance, era, set-piece, pipe, junction (router), surge — Mini Motorways lineage / plumbing metaphor /
+  user-ruled topology terminology; they make no networking claim).
+- **Renames ruled (lavish verdict 2026-08-15, session 36b4f1ff33e248bd).**
+  - **drop ladder → drop precedence** — RFC 2597 AF: within a class, drop order *is* drop precedence — BE sheds
+    first, the next victim only once the lower rung is exhausted (the E9 shed loop, `core/flow.odin`).
+  - **strain → congestion / utilization** — RFC 2309 congestion; the metric was always utilization vs throughput.
+    Applies to `Strain_Level` → `Congestion_Level`, `Warning_Sign.Node_Strained` → `Node_Congested`, the
+    `node_strain`/`pipe_strain` state, the `node_strained_lead_ticks` balance key, the strain-heatmap (8.1) surface.
+  - **lane → class queue, TWO-TIER** — the per-pipe bandwidth partition is mechanically a DiffServ **class queue**
+    (RFC 2475; CBQ/WFQ); docs/architecture/comments name it so. The player-facing surface, HUD, and core identifiers
+    keep **lane** (the 2026-08-12 spatial-lane visual + the EF/AF/DF class names stand).
+  - **pressure → congestion** — the pipe warning (`Warning_Sign.Pipe_Pressure` → `Pipe_Congested`,
+    `pipe_pressure_lead_ticks` balance key); the plumbing-metaphor gloss ("pipes / pressure / leaks / valves",
+    GDD §M4 metaphor boundary) remains in prose where it names the metaphor itself.
+  - **Pressure_Plan → Demand_Plan** — the demand director's forecast plan is a demand schedule, not pressure
+    (matches `demand.json`/`DemandSpec`); `scripted_plan_pressure` → `scripted_plan_demand`,
+    `growth_plan_pressure` → `growth_plan_demand`.
+  - **Cmd_Set_Emphasis → Cmd_Set_Weights** — the 5.8 panel payload is the weight set; the tag constant
+    `CMD_TAG_SET_WEIGHTS` keeps value 5 (the wire is untouched).
+- **Rename-PR discipline (binds future stories, incl. the queued visibility job's HUD — its surfaces use these
+  terms).**
+  - Serialized contracts + LOG_VERSION untouched — the wire format is value/layout (numeric writers, numeric tag
+    constants), so identifier renames are byte-neutral by proof; T1/replay byte-identity proven in the PR body.
+  - balance.json key renames fold catalog_hash → this PR's **deliberate T1 re-bless** (the only golden shift; the
+    splice proof shows the old catalog_hash field reproduces the old tick-1 hashes).
+  - Rendered HUD-string changes are deliberate T2 folds, listed in the PR (the strain legend at `app/main.odin:1197`
+    now reads "node congestion …" — the harness capture path never renders the HUD, so no T2 pixel moved).
+  - Phase-2 rename PR serialized behind 5.2's merge (merged 2026-08-15, PR #54 — comment-level overlap resolved).
